  "document": "Cinestill\nCinestill Film creates photographic film for still cameras from Kodak's motion picture cinema film. Cinestill Film uses a modified version of Kodak motion picture cinema film, allowing it to be developed with the C-41 process rather than the Eastman Color Negative process. Beta testing of Cinestill Film's \"800Tungsten Xpro C-41\" began in late 2012, the film is based on Kodak's \"Vision 3 5219\" motion picture cinema film. Although the \"Vision 3 5219\" film is normally rated for 500ISO, the conversion to C-41 processing allows the film to be rated at 800ISO."
